---
/**
 * NarrativeSections - Long-form sections below the MRS slab.
 * Numbered eyebrow + H2 + body copy per section. Five sections total:
 * show it running, one plugin, how it ships, learn, open source.
 *
 * Mirrors handoff Narrative.jsx.
 */
import Container from "@/components/ui/container.astro";
import Grid from "@/components/ui/grid.astro";
import Card from "@/components/ui/card.astro";
import CardHeader from "@/components/ui/card-header.astro";
import CardTitle from "@/components/ui/card-title.astro";
import CardDescription from "@/components/ui/card-description.astro";
import H2 from "@/components/ui/typography-h2.astro";
import P from "@/components/ui/typography-p.astro";
import Code from "@/components/ui/typography-code.astro";
import Codeblock from "@/components/ui/typography-codeblock.astro";
import { SQLITE_CONFIG, SQLITE_DRY_RUN, SQLITE_PUSH, TURSO_CONFIG } from "@/src/data/captures";
---

<div class="bg-background">
    <Container size="5xl" padding="20" gap="20">

        <section>
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">01 &middot; show it running</div>
            <H2>A TOML file, a dry-run, a push.</H2>
            <P size="display-small">The whole product in thirty seconds. Real CLI output, captured against the Westwind sample in the repository. No mockups.</P>

            <Codeblock>{SQLITE_CONFIG}</Codeblock>

            <Codeblock>{SQLITE_DRY_RUN}</Codeblock>

            <Codeblock>{SQLITE_PUSH}</Codeblock>

            <P size="display-small" color="muted-foreground">The dry-run writes nothing. The push writes exactly what the dry-run described. Same counts; the lines come out in the order the set iterates. No surprises.</P>
        </section>

        <section id="targets">
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">02 &middot; one plugin, any LIKE backend</div>
            <H2>Eight profiles ship today. A backend that fits an existing request shape is config, not a fork.</H2>
            <P size="display-small">Every remote target smugglr reaches over HTTP goes through one plugin, <Code>smugglr-http-sql</Code>. Pick a built-in profile by name and swapping targets is a config change, not a recompile.</P>

            <Codeblock>{`d1            # Cloudflare D1 (not reachable in 0.5.0: smugglr#429, #430, #436)
turso         # Turso / libSQL
rqlite        # rqlite
datasette     # Datasette
starbasedb    # StarbaseDB
sqlite-cloud  # SQLite Cloud
http-sql      # http-sql wire spec
generic       # flat {sql, params} JSON`}</Codeblock>

            <P size="display-small">This one points at Turso. <Code>name</Code> is the plugin binary; the vendor is the <Code>profile</Code>:</P>
            <Codeblock>{TURSO_CONFIG}</Codeblock>

            <P size="display-small" color="muted-foreground">Same config file, same commands, same diff engine, different profile. A backend whose HTTP requests match the generic or http-sql shape works by pointing at that profile in config. A backend that speaks a genuinely new request or response shape needs a new profile in the core, which is a contribution rather than just a config edit.</P>

            <P size="display-small">Every hosted target needs the second binary, <Code>smugglr-http-sql</Code>: <Code>cargo install smugglr-http-sql</Code>, or the release archive, which carries it beside <Code>smugglr</Code> from 0.5.1.</P>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">03 &middot; how it ships</div>
            <H2>Same algorithm, same adapters, same verbs.</H2>
            <P size="display-small"><Code>cargo install smugglr</Code> for the native CLI and <Code>cargo install smugglr-http-sql</Code> for the hosted backends, with pre-built binaries for macOS, Linux x64, and Windows. <Code>cargo add smugglr-core</Code> to embed the engine in a Rust service. <Code>pnpm add smugglr</Code> for the WebAssembly build in a browser or in Node. Same diff engine, same verbs, same summary block on every path.</P>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">04 &middot; learn</div>
            <H2>Four entry points for the 10% reading this as a human.</H2>
            <Grid columns={2} gap="4">
                <a href="/get-started/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>Get Started <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Five minutes to your first push.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
                <a href="/docs/cli-reference/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>CLI Reference <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Every command, every flag, every exit code.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
                <a href="/docs/configuration/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>Configuration <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>The complete config.toml.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
                <a href="/docs/how-it-works/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>How It Works <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Content hashing, the sync algorithm, the relay.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
            </Grid>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">05 &middot; compare</div>
            <H2>Two reads of the same comparison.</H2>
            <P size="display-small">Honest, falsifiable, no marketing. Where smugglr fits next to Litestream, rqlite, ElectricSQL, PowerSync, Firebase, Supabase Realtime, and the rest. Game devs get a separate page that names Photon, Colyseus, Mirror, and the persistent tier behind a netcode framework.</P>
            <Grid columns={2} gap="4">
                <a href="/compare/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>compare <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Sync engines, hosted services, the client-cache layer. The general read.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
                <a href="/compare/games/" class="group hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
                    <Card>
                        <CardHeader>
                            <CardTitle>compare / games <span class="text-muted-foreground">&#8599;</span></CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Photon, Colyseus, Mirror, and the persistent layer every game needs.</CardDescription>
                        </CardHeader>
                    </Card>
                </a>
            </Grid>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="font-heading font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3.5 pt-3.5 border-t border-foreground">06 &middot; open source</div>
            <H2>MIT licensed. All of it.</H2>
            <P size="display-small">The CLI, the core engine, the plugin system. On <a href="https://github.com/rafters-studio/smugglr" class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground transition-colors">github.com/rafters-studio/smugglr</a>.</P>
        </section>

    </Container>
</div>
